request.description:
This endpoint allows you to update a specific ruleset using the HTTP PUT method. The request should be sent to [http://localhost:{{port}}/ruleset/{{ruleset-id}}](http://localhost:{{port}}/ruleset/9).

### Request Body

The request should include a JSON payload in the raw request body type with the following structure:

``` json
{
    "id": 0,
    "name": "",
    "creation_date": "",
    "rules": [
        {
            "id": 0,
            "priority": 0,
            "event_type": "",
            "conditions": [
                {
                    "id": 0,
                    "fact_type": "",
                    "value_type": ""
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

 ```

All fields must be filled appropriately, and will result in a bad status code and unsuccessful execution if you fail to satisfy them.

When you are updating a ruleset and are adding a new rule or condition, you do not include the "id" field inside of the new rule or condition.

This endpoint is an extended version of our "GetAllRulesets", with the difference being this will give every detail for everything in our database. ((this was created for Deep))

